INT. CLOSED PLANETARIUM - NIGHT

A domed room. Rows of empty reclining seats. A projector hums in the center, casting a slow field of stars across the ceiling.

A man in a damp raincoat stands at the control console. He wipes his hands on a handkerchief, one finger at a time.

A WOMAN enters from the lobby door, keys in her hand. She stops. She does not turn on the lights.

STRANGER
Evening.

She sets her keys on the nearest seat, carefully, so they make no sound.

WOMAN
We're closed.

STRANGER
So I see.

He nudges a dial. The stars drift. A comet crosses the dome.

WOMAN
Door was locked.

STRANGER
It was.

He smiles at the ceiling. She watches his hands.

WOMAN
You want something to drink? There's a kettle in the office.

STRANGER
Kind of you.

She does not move toward the office. Neither does he.

WOMAN
Your coat's wet.

STRANGER
It's been a long walk.

WOMAN
From where?

He lets the question hang. The comet fades.

STRANGER
You kept the Orion show. They told me you'd cut it.

WOMAN
Who told you?

STRANGER
Man at the ticket window. Years ago.

She takes one step down the aisle. He takes one up. They stop level with the fourth row.

WOMAN
I don't think I know you.

STRANGER
No. But your husband did.

Her jaw sets. She glances at the exit sign, then back.

WOMAN
My husband's dead.

STRANGER
That's what I said. Did.

She reaches slowly into her coat pocket. He watches it. She pulls out a small brass key and holds it up between two fingers.

WOMAN
Basement. Where he kept the film reels.

STRANGER
(softly)
I thought so.

WOMAN
He wrote a name on every can. Yours is on the third shelf.

He doesn't answer. The stars wheel overhead.

WOMAN (CONT'D)
Tell me your name and I'll hand you the key.

A long beat. He folds the handkerchief into a square.

STRANGER
Desmond Pryce.

WOMAN
Thank you, Mr. Pryce.

She places the key on the armrest between them. He doesn't reach for it.

DESMOND
Aren't you going to ask what's on the reel?

WOMAN
No.

She picks up her own keys again. Turns toward the lobby. Stops with her back to him.

WOMAN (CONT'D)
The lights come on at eleven. You have twenty minutes.

She leaves. The door sighs shut.

He stands alone beneath Orion. Then he takes the key.
